[verification-budget
  [; The verification-cost BOUNDS (#1562, RULED: VCOST-1). The owner's sentence
     — "the fixture grader ≤ 20 min, a selected post-merge run ≤ 20 min, the
     union ≤ 60 min" — has to be a step or it is a wish, and a step needs the
     numbers in one place with the measurement that set each and the issue that
     last moved it.

     A bound moves ONLY in a commit that names why, and never to make a run
     pass: raising one because a run exceeded it is the ratchet running
     backwards, and `check-verification-budget` says so in its own refusal. ]

  [bound name=fixture-grader seconds=1200
    [what 'make fixtures, unselected — the seven grader shards over the whole module corpus']
    [measured '1,384 s census on 2026-09-17; connector.cxd alone 2,898 s under load after #1515 (3,168 s before), which is why the shard split and the shared parse both count toward this row']
    [moved-by 1515]
    [note 'the residue is 260 harness cases waiting out real bounds — 89% of connector.cxd. Lowering this row further is #1515s letter, not a tightening here.']]

  [bound name=selected-run seconds=9263
    [what 'a SELECTED post-merge run — make test-changed BASE=<last passed head> plus the branch steps it selects']
    [measured '154 min 23 s on the selected run on 884c05469, idle box (load 1.81), 2026-09-19 19:52Z — the first row the loop wrote; the row is raised to that measured value on the owner'"'"'s word of 2026-09-21 and ratchets DOWN only from here']
    [moved-by 1561]
    [note 'the profile tail is the other half: #1560 makes it grade only what the change touches.']]

  [bound name=union seconds=10516
    [what 'make test — the whole TEST_TARGETS union, the merge gate']
    [measured '175 min 16 s on the full union on 57745f541, idle box (load 1.46), 2026-09-19 21:40Z — the first row the loop wrote; raised to the measured value on the owner'"'"'s word of 2026-09-21, ratchets DOWN only; the 60-min target stands as the goal #1561 and the profile-gate sharding reach']
    [moved-by 1561]
    [note 'the compile ratio is the open half: 648 CPU-min compiling against 205 running, 80 standalone test files. #1561 is what moves this row.']]
]
